    "Notes Updated": "5/23/2023",
    "Scouting Notes": "Offensive Notes\n Swing is pretty smooth looking for a guy his size, has some Yelich to his finish.\n Likely will struggle with grounders a bit due to the swing, but should have the barrel in the zone a long time.\n Big raw power, hoping he can get to it in games.\n Better hit tool than one would expect at his size.\n Raw, but a lot of potential, with decent bat to ball skills.\nPitching Notes\n Fastball is lively, and could gain more velo as he continues to mature. Would not be surprised to see triple digits in the future. (Update as of April, 2023: He is hitting triple digits now)\n Breaking ball looked sharp in the video I've seen.\n Have heard changeup is fringey, but flashes average.\n Command and control are pretty rough currently, if he can even be fringe average he will be a really fun pitcher.\nOverall\n I wouldn't be surprised to see the two way experiment last for a while. He shows a pretty high ceiling on both sides of the ball.\n If I had to choose, I'd guess that he ends up on the mound due to the insane liveliness of his stuff. Like I said though, I'd prefer that they continue to give him a shot at both.",
